'' A goroutine with 64 KiB of locals and a runtime call under them survives (tiko-studio
'' TS-006). The defect was Linux only -- a worker's 16 KiB PTHREAD_STACK_MIN stack, exit 139
'' -- and the suite runs RUN tests on Windows only, so here this guards the Windows side and
'' the shared scheduler path; the Linux A/B is the same source with -target linux-x86_64,
'' linked and run under WSL.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 -mt tests/codegen/src/spawn-worker-stack.tiko -o tests/codegen/spawnworkerstack.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/codegen/spawnworkerstack.exe
'' RUN: tests/codegen/spawnworkerstack.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: goroutine survived: 255
